    ('b5494a21-b48f-454f-b0c7-687274173f4c'::uuid, 'site_type', 'Fortress/citadel', 'Settlement', 'fields-wd1-2026-09-26b-s008:b5494a21-b48f-454f-b0c7-687274173f4c:site_type', 'fields-wd1-2026-09-26b-s008 (wd1-replace): ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Settlement''', '[{"source": "https://www.thecollector.com/celts-portugal/", "url": "https://www.thecollector.com/celts-portugal/", "quote": "another significant Celtic settlement: Citânia de Sabroso. This archaeological site, classified as a National Monument, includes a group of around 39 circular and rectangular houses surrounded by walls.", "outcome": "found"}, {"source": "https://msarmento.org/espacos/castro-de-sabroso/", "url": "https://msarmento.org/espacos/castro-de-sabroso/", "quote": "Trata-se de um impressionante conjunto de ruínas de um povoado fortificado da segunda metade do I milénio a. C., com uma extensão de cerca de três hectares.", "outcome": "found"}, {"source": "WD1 decision (counted, round 1, wd1-r1-b0020)", "decision": "replace", "status": "MISSING", "reasoning": "Castro de Sabroso (Citânia de Sabroso, São Lourenço de Sande, Guimarães) is an Iron Age castro: The Collector calls it a Celtic settlement of about 39 houses surrounded by walls, and the Sociedade Martins Sarmento, which looks after the site, calls it the ruins of a povoado fortificado (fortified settlement) of the second half of the 1st millennium BC. Both describe a walled settlement lived in by a community, not a purely military fortress or citadel, so the stored Fortress/citadel is replaced by Settlement.", "value_page": null}]'::jsonb),
